(32, 'Kirsty Gregory', 'kirsty.gregory2019@outlook.com', '07703911025', 'Hi, I am interested in the Sound Healing Course. I am confused with prices. \r\nRegistration Fee £300 \r\nDouble Sharing Fee £795 \r\n= £1,096 in total for the course.\r\n\r\nOr £795 - £300 = £495 to pay when I arrive at the centre? ', 'Website Form', '2025-09-09 00:41:03'),
(33, 'Catia', 'catoaleite1@gmail.com', '', 'Hi there\r\n\r\nI hope this email finds you well .\r\nI’m traveling to Rishikesh in December and I’m looking for a yoga retreat from the 13-20 of December intermediate level yoga meditation pranayama - based on the eight limbs of yoga. Wondering if you have anything going on on these dates?\r\n\r\nOr if you can recommend?\r\n\r\nI look very much forward to hearing back from you.\r\n\r\nWith gratitude\r\nCatia ', 'Website Form', '2025-09-13 01:22:38'),
(34, 'Tanya Lee', 'tanya.lee@mail.mcgill.ca', '07519740115', 'Hello,\r\n\r\nI wanted to ask about the dual certification for the 300hr course + Sound healing training. Is the sound healing course always held on the 24th of ever month, or is it a different course if pursuing the dual certification?\r\n\r\nI also wanted to about accommodation. I see online that there are only double or triple options, however in several of Adhiroha&#39;s videos it appears that there are private rooms- is this a possibility?\r\n\r\nThank you!\r\n\r\nTanya', 'Website Form', '2025-09-13 07:21:30'),
(35, 'Isabella', 'isabellachemeri@gmail.com', '+39 3290869539', 'Dear All, I hope you are fine.\r\nI am very interested in taking part of this journey, specifically for the 200 hours, however I have some food allergies and I would like to know if it is possible to have dishes who takes this into account and if I need to pay extra money for these requests. I cannot eat gluten (such as in white and brown flour) and lactose as in milk (I can drink vegetable milk  though). \r\nIn addition, I would like to know what other expenses are not included so I can be prepared since I come from Italy.\r\n\r\nthanks for your help.\r\nWaiting for your feedback.\r\n\r\nbest,', 'Website Form', '2025-09-15 18:37:29'),
(36, 'Camila Cortes Bustamante', 'cortes.camila13@gmail.com', '56926419995', 'My name is Camila Cortés, and I am very interested in joining your 200-hour yoga teacher training course scheduled for May 2026.\r\n\r\nI would like to share that I have an obstetric brachial plexus injury in my left arm, which means that sometimes I may need adaptations in certain asanas. Nevertheless, I am highly motivated and committed to the practice, and I deeply appreciate any support or modifications that could be considered.\r\n\r\nI have practiced Hatha Yoga in my home country, Chile, and I would love to deepen my learning and training as a teacher. In addition, my native language is Spanish, and my English level is B2. I would like to know if you offer classes with Spanish translation, as it is very important for me to fully absorb all the knowledge during the training.\r\n\r\nI would be very grateful if you could share more details about the course, requirements, and the registration process.\r\n\r\nWith gratitude,\r\nCamila Cortés', 'Website Form', '2025-10-01 12:29:22'),
(37, 'Craig Byrd', 'cnbyrdgoo@gmail.com', '+01 5056001415', 'Greetings\r\nI have been investigating several sessions in Rishikesh next year and have decided to to them all at Adhiroha.  I plan on starting with Sound Bath training on 24 September 26 and following with the 300 hour YTT month of October.  I would like to take the Ayurveda wellness retreat for the beginning week of November.  \r\nThe registration is not yet open for the October 300 hour YTT, and I see there is a discount for adding the Sound Bath training.  I plan on double occupancy accommodations.  I would like to secure my place for the three sessions together as soon as all of the registrations are available.  It seems I should wait until next month to do this. \r\nI also would like to investigate renting a guitar for the seven weeks   if you have a recommendation for that.  I am a performing songwriter and cannot go the whole period without practice.  There are also several days before the wellness retreat starts when no training occurs.  Would lodging continue through those days? I may want to rent a vehicle of take a public transportation to do some sightseeing if you have some ideas about that.\r\nThank you for your consideration of my issues.  I look forward to spending my time in India with you.\r\nRegards\r\nCB', 'Website Form', '2025-10-01 22:37:36'),
(38, 'julia Markovic', 'juliamarkovic@yahoo.co.uk', '07908201274', 'Hello, I note that the day begins at 5.45am, and ends at 22.00, as someone that has insomnia issues, and spinal challenges, I wonder if there will be enough hours of rest, and whether the bed mattresses will be suitable for my spine (medium firm) I am 58 years old, but very mobile apart from these issues. I have been practicing yoga for many years, but with the foundation of good sleep!\r\nMany thanks,\r\nJulia', 'Website Form', '2025-10-03 01:09:08'),
(39, 'Suman Sharma', 'suman.16888@gmail.com', '07738580001', 'Hello..I want to know about upcoming 300hr Yttc course with fees for indian students... thankyou ', 'Website Form', '2025-10-08 13:43:08'),
