\n\nMantras: Experience the calming and consciousness-elevating effects of sacred sounds.\nPranayama: Learn breath control techniques to enhance lung capacity and respiratory health.\nShatkarma: Purify the body and mind with cleansing practices like nasal cleansing and skull shining breath.\nHatha Yoga: Focus on physical postures, breathing, and meditation for strength, flexibility, and balance.\nAshtanga Vinyasa: Dynamic yoga synchronizing breath with movement to build strength and flexibility.\nYoga Anatomy: Understand skeletal, muscular, and respiratory systems and their relation to yoga postures.\nYoga Philosophy: Explore ancient texts like the Yoga Sutras and Bhagavad Gita, diving into yoga\'s philosophical aspects.\nMeditation: Practice mindfulness, mantra, and guided visualisation techniques for mental calm and focus.\nAdjustment & Alignment: Utilise props in the Iyengar technique to enhance posture precision and deepen your practice.\n\nRegarding assessment, there will be a written test and practical teaching sessions at the end of the course. In addition, ongoing evaluation methods such as assignments, practical sessions, mock teaching, and oral Q&A will be conducted based on individual subject instructors\' discretion. Whether it\'s a final exam or continuous assessment, our goal is to ensure alignment with the course objectives and provide a fair evaluation of your learning progress.\n\nWe hope this addresses your questions. Please feel free to contact us for any further queries or clarifications. We\'re committed to supporting you throughout your journey with us.\n\nLooking forward to welcoming you to our Adhiroha community!\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n* Manual Follow Up 1\n\nAum Namaha Shivaya!\n\nDear [Name],\n\nWe hope this email finds you well.\n\nI am your assigned course counsellor for the 200 Hour YTTC in Rishikesh for [Month, Year]. We wanted to ensure you received all the information r